## Intent & Decisions
The user requested reviewing all five rules one at a time, consulting the
GPT-6 Astra and Claude Fable prompting guidance, then consolidating into one
repository file symlinked for both Codex and Claude rather than Claude rules.
We interviewed each meaningful decision boundary before drafting.

Accepted decisions: prefer representations that eliminate special cases
(Torvalds linked-list example); autonomously restructure across callers and
investigate/delete unrelated unnecessary code, separated into logical gh-stack
changes or independent stacks. Unexplained purpose no longer vetoes deletion:
use independent fresh-context reviewers, continue discovery to a clear majority
on current evidence, but demonstrated functional/behavioral failure overrides
votes. Tests may protect implementation details; determine whether the asserted
behavior actually contributes to correctness before changing them. Reproduce
bugs before fixes; automated regression preferred, repeatable script/controlled
experiment accepted. Duplication may reveal the right abstraction; third-use
is a heuristic. Follow local patterns and note tradeoffs. Broad history/code/PR/
review/issue/Slack/Git-note research is opportunistic, never a required checklist.

Errors: validate boundaries, enforce invariants explicitly, bounded observable
recovery only when correct. Fail isolated work; terminate when shared state may
be corrupted unless safe continuation is established. Challenge/interview the
ask, then honor settled choices unless new evidence appears. Brief design for
costly choices, simple disposable experiments preferred. Performance optimization
requires explicit ask; incidental automation stays temporary commands.

Comments default none, including package/function docs unless requested or
repo-required. Exceptional comments can protect non-obvious correctness
constraints. Remove extraneous comments, separately if needed for focused PRs.
History belongs in commit messages/notes. Frequent autonomous local commits;
notes on every commit; consolidate notes and commits to exactly one commit per
PR base. Autonomous pushes/draft PRs allowed, human decides readiness.

Claude MCP and I debated the note template: keep Errors separate from Attempts
to preserve candor; merge Hints and Discoveries; include consequential external
actions and verification. User accepted all six headings with None for empties.
STE otherwise stays unchanged; user explicitly removed humanizer dependency.

